{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/host/{text,hash}.cljc; sed -n '1,92p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/jolt/dao/host/hash.jolt; head -55 /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; cat build/p1c-r2/yin-after-b123.log; tail -12 build/p1c-r2/probe-gates.log\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.host.text\n  \"The host strings of the primitive profile\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A). A host string\n   is a sequence of UTF-16 code units on every host (JVM `String`, JS\n   string, Dart `String`).\n\n   Table A, kind P (§2.4): `unit-count`, `code-unit`, `units->string`,\n   `utf8-encode`, `utf8-decode`, `nfc`. Equal arguments give equal\n   results on every host:\n   - `utf8-encode` refuses an unpaired surrogate `:unpaired-surrogate`\n     instead of substituting (the JVM's `?`, U+FFFD elsewhere), so the\n     bytes of every string it accepts are identical on every host; it\n     returns fresh bytes the caller holds the mutation right to.\n   - `utf8-decode` is strict RFC 3629: an overlong form, an encoded\n     surrogate, a code point above U+10FFFF or a truncated sequence is\n     refused `:invalid-utf8`, never decoded to U+FFFD; a leading BOM is\n     content. It is the decoder of `dao.jing.cbor` (`utf8`), extracted.\n   - `nfc` is Unicode Normalization Form C (`java.text.Normalizer`,\n     `String.prototype.normalize`, the `unorm_dart` package); the profile\n     pins Unicode 16.0 (§2.5).\n\n   Table B, P, no host arm: `code-points`, over `unit-count` and\n   `code-unit` (the private `yin.vm.data` helper, made public here).\n\n   Oracle: `dao.host.text-test` and the text rows of table D, re-asserted\n   by `dao.host.conformance-test`. A refusal throws `ex-info` whose data\n   carries `:dao.host/refusal`, a class keyword, and `:dao.host/entry`.\n   Every reader conditional names `:cljd` first, because the ClojureDart\n   build also reads `:clj`.\"\n  #?@(:cljd [(:require [\"dart:convert\" :as convert]\n                       [\"package:unorm_dart/unorm_dart.dart\" :as unorm])\n             (:import [\"dart:core\" FormatException String]\n                      [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])]\n      :clj [(:import (java.nio ByteBuffer)\n                     (java.nio.charset CharacterCodingException CodingErrorAction\n                                       StandardCharsets))]))\n\n\n(defn- refuse\n  [entry cls detail]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" \" (name cls) \" (\" detail \")\")\n                  {:dao.host/refusal cls :dao.host/entry entry :detail detail})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Code units\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn unit-count\n  \"P. The number of UTF-16 code units of string `s`.\"\n  [s]\n  #?(:cljd (.-length ^String s)\n     :clj (.length ^String s)\n     :cljs (.-length s)))\n\n\n(defn code-unit\n  \"P. The UTF-16 code unit at index `i` of `s`, 0 to 0xFFFF; the caller\n   has checked 0 <= i < `unit-count`.\"\n  [s i]\n  #?(:cljd (.codeUnitAt ^String s i)\n     :clj (int (.charAt ^String s (int i)))\n     :cljs (.charCodeAt s i)))\n\n\n(defn units->string\n  \"P. The host string of the UTF-16 code units `units` (each 0 to\n   0xFFFF), unpaired surrogates included.\"\n  [units]\n  #?(:cljd (let [sb (StringBuffer)]\n             (doseq [u units] (.writeCharCode sb u))\n             (.toString sb))\n     :clj (let [sb (StringBuilder.)]\n            (doseq [u units] (.append sb (char u)))\n            (.toString sb))\n     :cljs (let [a (array)]\n             (doseq [u units] (.push a (.fromCharCode js/String u)))\n             (.join a \"\"))))\n\n\n(defn- high-surrogate?\n  [u]\n  (<= 0xD800 u 0xDBFF))\n\n\n(defn- low-surrogate?\n  [u]\n  (<= 0xDC00 u 0xDFFF))\n\n\n(defn code-points\n  \"P, table B. The code points of string `s` as a vector: a surrogate\n   pair decodes to one code point, an unpaired surrogate is its own.\"\n  [s]\n  (let [n (unit-count s)]\n    (loop [i 0\n           out (transient [])]\n      (if (< i n)\n        (let [u (code-unit s i)\n              v (when (< (inc i) n) (code-unit s (inc i)))]\n          (if (and (high-surrogate? u) v (low-surrogate? v))\n            (recur (+ i 2)\n                   (conj! out (+ 0x10000\n                                 (* (- u 0xD800) 0x400)\n                                 (- v 0xDC00))))\n            (recur (inc i) (conj! out u))))\n        (persistent! out)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; UTF-8\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- check-surrogates!\n  \"Refuse `:unpaired-surrogate` unless every surrogate of `s` is paired.\"\n  [entry s]\n  (let [n (unit-count s)]\n    (loop [i 0]\n      (when (< i n)\n        (let [c (code-unit s i)]\n(ns dao.host.hash\n  \"The jolt override of src/cljc/dao/host/hash.cljc (the :jolt alias puts\n   src/jolt first, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §4.2, §6.2,\n   §6.3): the same public entries, arities, docstrings and refusal data\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A).\n\n   P entries (§2.4): `blake3-bytes` and `sha256-bytes`. They take host\n   bytes (jolt's byte array) and return fresh host bytes representing the\n   32-byte digest (256 bits). They leave their arguments unmodified.\n\n   Both are `:blocking` calls into native/jolt-crypto, which `bb\n   build:jolt-native` builds: BLAKE3 is the vendored upstream C reference,\n   SHA-256 the declared system libcrypto's EVP API. The input is copied into\n   caller-owned native memory (never a C string, so embedded NUL is data),\n   the digest is read back into a fresh jolt byte array, and the memory is\n   freed on every path: each native acquisition owns its own release,\n   established as soon as it is acquired (`with-native`), so a later\n   allocation or copy that fails still frees every earlier buffer, and each\n   free runs whether or not another failed.\n\n   Loading this namespace is the provenance gate (§6.3): it refuses, by\n   throwing, unless the wrapper writes this namespace's layout and reports\n   that every EVP entry resolved to exactly the library jolt-toolchain.edn\n   qualified for this platform (:native :libcrypto :qualified): the same\n   canonical real path (which the declared :path must also resolve to), the\n   same OpenSSL_version_num and the same file SHA-256, at no lower than\n   :min-version. An upgrade, a repointed link or a replaced file therefore\n   fails until requalified (the procedure is in jolt-toolchain.edn). No\n   digest is computed before that check passes; a missing library fails the\n   load.\n\n   String digesting is a table B portable composition over `dao.host.text`\n   and these byte primitives (`blake3`, `sha256`, `digest-string`,\n   `digest-bytes`), hosted in `dao.jing`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    [jolt.ffi :as ffi]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The native library and its provenance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private platform\n  ;; as yang.antlr.cst decides it: jolt's os.name/os.arch shim can answer\n  ;; nil, which reads as Linux and x86_64\n  (let [os (str/lower-case (or (System/getProperty \"os.name\") \"\"))\n        arch (System/getProperty \"os.arch\")]\n    (str (if (str/includes? os \"mac\") \"darwin\" \"linux\") \"-\"\n         (if (#{\"aarch64\" \"arm64\"} arch) \"arm64\" \"x86_64\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private library\n  ;; the wrapper `bb build:jolt-native` builds, under the working directory\n  (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\") \"/build/native/\" platform\n       \"/jolt-crypto/lib/libjolt_crypto\"\n       (if (str/starts-with? platform \"darwin\") \".dylib\" \".so\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private libcrypto-declaration\n  (get-in (edn/read-string (slurp (str (System/getProperty \"user.dir\")\n                                       \"/jolt-toolchain.edn\")))\n          [:native :libcrypto]))\n\n\n(ffi/load-library library)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-layout-version \"jolt_crypto_layout_version\" [] :int)\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-provenance \"jolt_crypto_provenance\" [:pointer :size_t] :int)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-blake3 \"jolt_crypto_blake3\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-sha256 \"jolt_crypto_sha256\"\n            [:pointer :size_t :pointer] :int :blocking)\n\n\n;; 3 (J2): the random entry joined the exported set (jolt_crypto_random for\n;; yin.vm.linker.sign/generate's :jolt arm); a J1b-built wrapper answers 2 and\n;; is refused here rather than at a missing-symbol error in the linker.\n;; 4 (J6c): jolt_crypto_sha1 joined it (dao.stream.ws.crypto) and EVP_sha1\n;; the provenance audit; a J2-built wrapper answers 3 and is refused here.\n(def ^:private layout 4)\n\n\n(defn- refuse-load\n  [message data]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"jolt-crypto refused: \" message)\n                  (assoc data :library library))))\n(ns yin.repl\n  \"The local Yin shell for DaoStream: explicit state, synchronous steps.\n\n   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock, or namespace\n   global.  It holds the one shell value a driver threads: the evaluator beside\n   its separately-owned program media — `program-in`, which the macro\n   expander observes, and `program-out`, which the evaluator's own observer\n   watches (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md` §10.1) — the language, the value\n   history, the output medium with its cursor, and a per-medium ledger\n   recording the last outcome that medium answered.  Every function takes a\n   state and returns the next one.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [] :jolt [[jolt.scheme :as scheme]] :default [])\n            #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn]\n               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.pretty :as pretty]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n            [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n            [yin.repl.ast-index :as ast-index]\n            [yin.repl.index :as index]\n            [yin.repl.publication :as publication]\n            [yin.repl.query :as query]\n            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.repl.state :as config]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]\n            [yin.vm.linker.pair :as link]\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [dao.space.index :as space-index]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]))\n\n\n(def output-capacity\n  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned output medium, in elements.\"\n  4096)\n\n\n(def ingress-capacity\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p;1196,1257p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/jolt/yin/repl/host.jolt; sed -n '1,145p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc; rg -n 'ns-meta|alter-meta\"'!|set-ns-meta|reset-meta!'\"' jolt-core/clojure/core/30-macros.clj host/chez/{ns.ss,natives-meta.ss} | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p;1196,1257p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/jolt/yin/repl/host.jolt; sed -n '1,145p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc; rg -n 'ns-meta|alter-meta\"'!|set-ns-meta|reset-meta!'\"' jolt-core/clojure/core/30-macros.clj host/chez/{ns.ss,natives-meta.ss} | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.repl.main\n  \"Host entry points for the DaoStream Yin REPL.\n\n   The one thing this namespace adds to `yin.repl.driver` is cadence, which\n   the DaoStream contract leaves to the runtime.  Per host, a line producer\n   appends what was typed to the input medium, nudges the step owner's wake\n   source, and returns; one ticker owns the state value and calls\n   `repl-step` serially at the interval `cadence-step` computes.  There is\n   no second state owner, and no line handler evaluates, requests, polls,\n   or prints.\n\n   A storage composition past the engine's own two stores reaches this\n   driver as plain data — the `composition` of `startup`'s options — and is\n   never named here: no transport, no peer, no publisher key file, no\n   `--index-store` scheme of its own past `mem` and `file:<dir>`, and no\n   flag of a composition's it parses itself.  The host entry point that\n   carries a composition supplies it (`yin.shell.main`); a host that\n   carries none drives the engine alone.  Every key of that value is\n   optional, and an absent one is the engine's own behaviour, so this\n   namespace has exactly one dependency direction: a composition may\n   require it, and it requires no composition.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:async\" :as async]\n                       [\"dart:convert\" :as convert]\n                       [\"dart:core\" :as dart-core]\n                       [\"dart:io\" :as io]]\n                :jolt [[yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n                       [yin.repl.host.common :as host-common]])\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.stream.waitset.cadence :as cadence]\n            [dao.stream.waitset.driver :as wake]\n            [yin.repl :as shell]\n            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]\n            [yin.repl.driver :as driver]\n            [yin.repl.host :as host]\n            [yin.repl.serve :as serve]\n            [yin.repl.state :as state]\n            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]))\n\n\n(def tick-millis\n  \"The base cadence of the single step owner.  Slow enough to cost nothing\n   while anything moves, fast enough that a remote result prints without\n   waiting for a keystroke.\"\n  25)\n\n\n(def default-cadence\n  \"The tick owner's idle curve.  `tick-millis` is the base interval, what a\n   wake resets to and what a pending write holds, and an idle composition\n   backs off doubling to 200 ms.  Local input and the explicit stop trigger\n   nudge the wake source, so operator actions never wait the curve out; a\n   lost nudge costs at most the armed interval.\"\n  {:poll-ms tick-millis\n   :backoff {:factor 2 :ceiling-ms 200}})\n\n\n(def prompt \"yin> \")\n\n\n(def telemetry-text\n  (str \"--telemetry and --telemetry-stream are not part of the DaoStream \"\n       \"REPL slice: the telemetry emit path is built (yin.vm.telemetry, opt-in \"\n       \"via the :telemetry {:stream ...} construction option (\"\n       \"yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md), but composing a sink into \"\n       \"this shell is not, so the flags are rejected rather than ignored\"))\n\n\n(defn parse-int\n  \"The decimal integer `text` names, or nil: total on every host.  At\n   most 15 digits, so the value is exact on every host (below 2^53) and\n   no host parser can overflow; a longer number is nil, which each flag\n   refuses as data.\n\n   A composition's flag parser reads this too (`yin.shell.cli`): one\n   integer grammar on every host, engine and composition alike.\"\n  [text]\n  (when (and (string? text) (re-matches #\"-?\\d{1,15}\" text))\n    #?(:cljd (int/parse text)\n       :cljs (js/parseInt text 10)\n       :clj (Long/parseLong text))))\n\n\n(defn- home-dir*\n  \"The user's home directory, or nil where the host has none (ClojureDart).\n   The node directory the saved state lives in is under it; a composition's\n   own subcommand paths are its own to derive (`yin.shell.cli`).\"\n  []\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj (System/getProperty \"user.home\")\n     :cljs (some-> js/process .-env .-HOME)))\n\n\n(defn plain-args\n  \"The plain form's `--name n` and `--dir d`, which name the node directory\n   its state file lives in (default `~/.yin/node`), removed from `args`.\n   Answers `[args extra]`.\"\n  [args]\n  (loop [args (seq args) rest [] node-name \"node\" dir nil]\n    (if-let [arg (first args)]\n      (case arg\n        \"--name\" (if (next args)\n                   (recur (nnext args) rest (second args) dir)\n                   (recur (next args) (conj rest arg) node-name dir))\n        \"--dir\" (if (next args)\n                  (recur (nnext args) rest node-name (second args))\n                  (recur (next args) (conj rest arg) node-name dir))\n        (recur (next args) (conj rest arg) node-name dir))\n      [rest {:name node-name :dir dir}])))\n\n\n(defn expand-args\n  \"Turn a subcommand surface into the flags `parse-args` reads, answering\n   `[args extra]`: `extra` carries what the arguments say beyond flags —\n   `:new-key` (a key file a subcommand makes), `:name` and `:dir` (the node\n   directory), and `:unset` (saved flags the subcommand clears).\n\n   The engine's own surface is the plain form alone (`plain-args`: `--name`\n   and `--dir`, which name the node directory the saved state lives in).  A\n   composition's subcommands are its own, and reach this driver as its\n   `:expand-args` hook — one that falls back to the plain form for anything\n   it does not own.  So a host carrying no composition has no subcommand\n   surface at all, and one carrying a composition never has this namespace\n   parse a word of it.\"\n  ([args] (expand-args args nil))\n  ([args composition]\n   ((or (:expand-args composition) plain-args) args)))\n\n\n(defn- parse-vm\n  \"A `--vm` value as the evaluator keyword the shell takes.\"\n  [text]\n  (let [vm-type (some-> text keyword)]\n    (if (contains? shell/vm-labels vm-type)\n      vm-type\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--vm takes one of \"\n                           (str/join \", \" (map name (sort (keys shell/vm-labels))))\n                           \", not \" (pr-str text))\n                      {:value text})))))\n\n\n(defn- parse-codec\n  \"A `--codec` value, `cbor` or `transit`, as the keyword `connect/codec-profiles`\n   names.\"\n  [value]\n  (let [k (some-> value keyword)]\n    (if (contains? connect/codec-profiles k)\n      k\n      (throw (ex-info (str #?(:cljd \"--codec takes cbor or transit, not \"\n                              :jolt \"--codec takes cbor, not \"\n                              :default \"--codec takes cbor or transit, not \") (pr-str value))\n                      {:value value})))))\n\n\n(defn parse-args\n  \"Parse the host arguments this driver owns.  `--telemetry` and\n   `--telemetry-stream` are rejected rather than ignored.  `--index-store`\n   is parsed into `:index-store-spec`: `:mem` (also what omission means),\n   or `{:type :file :dir dir}`; a missing value, an unknown scheme, or an\n   empty directory is refused here, by `yin.repl.store/parse-arg`, before\n   any host composes.\n\n   `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage composition\n   (`startup`'s option of the same name), and every way one widens this\n   surface arrives through it — statically, as data, on every host:\n\n   * `:parse-store-arg` parses an `--index-store` value over the engine's\n     schemes and the composition's own, so an operator's refusal names\n     every store this build can open;\n   * `:flag-parser` reads one flag this driver does not own:\n     `(f arg value args opts extra)` answers `{:opts opts' :extra extra'\n     :advance n}`, `n` the arguments consumed including the flag itself, or\n     nil for a flag it does not own, which this driver then reads itself;\n   * `:finalize` folds what the parse gathered into the resolved options,\n     `(f opts extra)`, once every argument has been read;\n   * `:initial-extra` is the accumulator `extra` starts as.\n\n   A host carrying no composition parses the engine's own flags and nothing\n   else, and an argument nobody owns is collected under `:extra` exactly as\n   it always was.\"\n  ([args] (parse-args args nil))\n  ([args composition]\n   (let [flag-parser (:flag-parser composition)\n         parse-store-arg (or (:parse-store-arg composition) store/parse-arg)\n         finalize (:finalize composition)]\n     (loop [args (seq args)\n            opts {:headless? false :host nil :port nil :rejected []\n                  :index-store-spec :mem}\n            extra (:initial-extra composition)]\n       (if-let [arg (first args)]\n         (let [value (second args)\n               hooked (when flag-parser\n                        (flag-parser arg value args opts extra))]\n           (if (some? hooked)\n             (recur (drop (:advance hooked 1) args)\n                    (or (:opts hooked) opts)\n                    (get hooked :extra extra))\n             (case arg\n               \"--port\" (recur (nnext args)\n                               (assoc opts :port (when-some [p (second args)]\n                                                   (let [n (parse-int p)]\n                                                     (if (and n (<= 0 n 65535))\n                                                       n\n                                                       (throw (ex-info\n                                                                (str \"--port takes a \"\n                                                                     \"port from 0 to \"\n                                                                     \"65535, not \"\n                                                                     (pr-str p))\n                                                                {:value p}))))))\n                               extra)\n               \"--host\" (throw (ex-info (str \"--host is gone: --port serves on all \"\n                                             \"interfaces, so it answers on \"\n                                             \"localhost and on this machine's IP\")\n                                        {}))\n               \"--codec\" (recur (nnext args)\n                                (assoc opts :codec (parse-codec value))\n                                extra)\n               \"--headless\" (recur (next args) (assoc opts :headless? true) extra)\n               \"--vm\" (recur (nnext args)\n     (defn -main\n       \"The engine's own JVM entry point: the `mem` and `file:<dir>` stores\n        and no storage composition.  The shipped product entry point is\n        `yin.shell.main/-main`, which supplies one.\"\n       [& args]\n       (main! args nil))))\n\n\n#?(:jolt\n   (do\n     (defn main!\n       \"One plain-thread owner. Stdin deposits only; EOF deposits (quit).\n        One host WebSocket instance serves the shell, a storage\n        composition's own endpoints and --port; every owner round polls its\n        sockets (headless included) and the instance is closed before exit,\n        however the drain ended.  Saved flags persist in the node\n        directory, as on the JVM (J4d): --reset forgets them and --no-state\n        neither reads nor writes them.\n\n        `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage\n        composition, nil for a host that carries none.\"\n       [args composition]\n       (let [adapter (host/websocket)\n             started (startup args {:persist? true :adapter adapter\n                                    :composition composition})]\n         (when (contains? started :exit) (exit-with! started))\n         (if-some [refusal (:refusal started)]\n           (refuse! refusal)\n           (let [{:keys [opts state server]} started\n                 headless? (boolean (:headless? opts))\n                 eof? (atom false)\n                 w (wake/make-wake)\n                 line! (fn [line]\n                         (if (nil? line)\n                           (do (reset! eof? true)\n                               (driver/submit-line! (:input state) \"(quit)\"))\n                           (driver/submit-line! (:input state) line)))\n                 sleep! (fn [ms]\n                          (wake/sleep-fds! w ms (:pump adapter)\n                                           (when-not (or headless? @eof?) line!)))]\n             (doseq [line (banner opts composition)] (println line))\n             (when-not headless? (print prompt))\n             (flush)\n             ;; the exit status leaves through System/exit, which skips the\n             ;; finally, so the exit path closes the instance itself too\n             (try\n               (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n                           sleep! (fn [status]\n                                    ((:close-host! adapter))\n                                    (wake/close! w)\n                                    (flush)\n                                    (System/exit status)))\n               (finally\n                 ((:close-host! adapter))\n                 (wake/close! w)))))))\n\n     (defn -main\n       \"The engine's own jolt entry point: the `mem` and `file:<dir>` stores\n        and no storage composition.  The shipped product entry point is\n        `yin.shell.main/-main`, which supplies one.\"\n       [& args]\n       (main! args nil))))\n(ns yin.repl.host\n  \"The jolt composition of the Yin REPL host WebSocket seam (J6e).\n\n   This jolt namespace shadows the `.cljc` one, so it carries only\n   `websocket`; the portable contract is `yin.repl.host.common`. It\n   composes the native RFC 6455 edge (`dao.stream.ws.jolt`) for the REPL:\n   upgrades reach `dao.stream.ws/accept-connection!` through the endpoint's\n   `accept!`, and each accepted connection reports through the\n   `dao.stream.ws/adapter` of its handle.\n\n   Unlike the JVM, Node and Dart packages, jolt's sockets move only when\n   their owner pumps them, so the adapter also carries `:pump` (the\n   driver's `{:interest :deadline :pump!}`, A2) and `:close-host!` (forced\n   cleanup once the owner loop has ended, A6). One instance per call: two\n   adapters never share a descriptor.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n            [dao.stream.ws.jolt :as wsj]))\n\n\n(defn websocket\n  \"Return a fresh jolt host adapter: `{:connect! :bind! :unbind! :pump\n   :close-host! :debug-state}` over one new instance. `opts` (tests only):\n   `:upgrade-timeout-ms`, `:close-deadline-ms`.\"\n  ([] (websocket nil))\n  ([opts]\n   (let [inst (wsj/create opts)]\n     {:connect! (fn [descriptor adapter] (wsj/connect! inst descriptor adapter))\n      :bind! (fn [options]\n               (wsj/bind! inst (assoc options :ws.jolt/adapter-of\n                                      #(some-> (:ws/handle %) ws/adapter))))\n      :unbind! (fn [listener deposit!] (wsj/unbind! inst listener deposit!))\n      :pump (wsj/host-pump inst)\n      :close-host! #(wsj/close-host! inst)\n      :debug-state #(wsj/debug-state inst)})))\n(ns yin.repl.host\n  \"The one seam between the Yin REPL and a real host WebSocket package.\n\n   `yin.repl.connect` and `yin.repl.serve` are complete compositions over\n   the DaoStream WebSocket boundary, which deliberately knows no socket\n   library: `dao.stream.ws/make-attacher` asks a host for `:connect!`, and a\n   listener is likewise host policy.  Each supported build composes that host\n   policy behind the same `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` value: this portable\n   namespace selects the JVM adapter, while host-specific `.cljs` and `.cljd`\n   shadows select Node and dart:io.\n\n   A shadow replaces this namespace wholesale, so it holds only `websocket` —\n   the one thing that differs per build.  The portable contract every build\n   shares lives in `yin.repl.host.common`.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd []\n                :jolt []\n                :clj [[yin.repl.host.jvm :as jvm]]\n                :default [])))\n\n\n(defn websocket\n  \"Return this build's host WebSocket adapter.\n\n   A conforming adapter is a map of:\n\n   * `:connect!` — `(fn [descriptor adapter] …)`, per\n     `dao.stream.ws/make-attacher`: it starts connecting, never waits, and\n     synchronously returns `{:send! … :close! …}`;\n   * `:bind!` — `(fn [{:keys [endpoint bind-host bind-port path accept! deposit!]}] …)`,\n     which binds a listener, routes each upgrade through\n     `(accept! request-path socket now)` with its own clock reading, and reports\n     every lifecycle fact through `deposit!` as plain data;\n   * `:unbind!` — `(fn [resources deposit!] …)`, which releases the listener and\n     whose close completion deposits `:stopped`.\"\n  []\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :jolt nil\n     :clj (jvm/websocket)\n     :default nil))\nhost/chez/ns.ss:873:    \"alter-meta!\" \"alter-var-root\" \"amap\" \"ancestors\" \"and\" \"any?\" \"apply\" \"areduce\"\nhost/chez/ns.ss:938:    \"replicate\" \"require\" \"requiring-resolve\" \"reset!\" \"reset-meta!\" \"reset-vals!\"\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1209:;; alter-meta! / reset-meta!: a var's metadata lives in the cell's meta field;\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1213:;; meta onto a fresh var — (alter-meta! v merge (meta macro-var)) — work. Marking\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1222:;; will never look, and the write is silently lost. clojure.core/alter-meta! and\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1223:;; reset-meta! ARE .alterMeta / .resetMeta on the JVM, so dispatch to the declared\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1228:(define (jolt-alter-meta! ref f . args)\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1243:(define (jolt-reset-meta! ref m)\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1332:(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"alter-meta!\" jolt-alter-meta!)\nhost/chez/ns.ss:1333:(def-var! \"clojure.core\" \"reset-meta!\" jolt-reset-meta!)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
